nd the ActRun framework that lets one activity run in a scene, in Class, in attract or in a hub round.\",\"Mixing six ways of drawing in one game (brawler, three-quarter, Mode 7, pseudo-3D road, a tilted tray, a side view) and keeping the camera, coordinates and input state straight when one scene hands over to another.\",\"Only the Dialog shadow patch: the name, text and choices used a fixed near-black shadow; they now read this.shadow so a bright dialog box can turn it off.\",\"Reset the camera (follow target, bounds, offset) on every scene change, or make game.go take effect at once in headless runs. Both would have saved debugging time.\"]\nd['promptFeedback']=[\"The tested recipes marked with a tick, with exact numbers and traps already found, plus a build order and a cut order. It made a very large game feel doable one milestone at a time.\",\"The title rule asks for a riff on the source's name while the plan says to avoid Wii names; the random pick was 'Wii Stork', so I kept the pick. The Lean tables were measured with a centred ring, but the Stork ring moves. The plan says engine v0.88.0 and the handoff was v0.89.0.\",\"The scope: twelve activities in six views, a local Class, an AI Hub ghost round, attract, dev mode, About, saves and a full test suite, all inside one session and its context.\",\"Mark which parts are required and which are stretch, give a rough size budget, and ship a small sample of the test harness (the vm loader, a bot loop and the brawler screen coordinates) so those do not have to be rediscovered.\"]\nd['aiHub']['description']=\"A deadpan five-day stay at a wellness retreat where one skill, your balance, drives twelve short exercises, coached by a needy talking scale and two wooden instructors. Local Class for up to four, and an AI Hub ghost round.\"\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=1,ensure_ascii=False)\njson.load(open(p)); print('ok')\nEOF\ncp exit-interview.json ../exit-interview.json; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='game/scenes/session.js'; s=