{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjMiyM2rGYUWvBwyxEMj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've nothing further to change. The Laundry Line set and the Stork tier 2 stars are back to the plan's values, and the remaining objections are not deviations from PLAN.md.\n\n- **Stork ring spacing:** PLAN.md says only that the ring \"moves to a new spot every 12 s\". It gives no distance and no tested number for it. The `ringR` value is my own choice, and I picked the smaller jump so that the plan's star thresholds and its tier 2 expectation both hold.\n- **Laundry Line:** the Lean set (`s 16, A 3.5`) is the plan's, and its band check passes with the plan's original expected values. Where the Laundry Line differs from the plan is course design, which the plan leaves open: shorter spans, a post every 3 m, and the sideways axis calmed inside the activity.\n- **Audio and controller:** these were checked as far as this computer allows, which the brief says is acceptable. Audio was checked through analysers and an `OfflineAudioContext` render, and the controller through a standard-mapping stub pad. The brief says anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\n- **1080p review:** I viewed the title, Plate, card, results and island at 1920×1080, along with most other screens.\n\nThe final build passes `node tests/run.mjs all`: 693 passed, 0 failed. The game file, `exit-interview.json` and `PROGRESS.md` are in the work folder. The Source Information and the three feedback sections are in my first reply and on the About screen."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":744,"cache_read_input_tokens":534826,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":744},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"inpu